# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Atelier Handbag App — Environment Variables Template
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file and rename it to `.env`
#   2. Fill in your actual values below
#   3. Restart the Expo dev server after changes (`npm start`)
#
# NOTE: All variables MUST start with EXPO_PUBLIC_ to be bundled into the app.
#       These values are embedded in the app bundle — do NOT put secret keys here.
#       Keep real API keys in your backend (e.g. n8n workflow), not in this file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── MockAPI (Product Data) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Create a free project at https://mockapi.io
# 2. Add a resource named "handbags" (see SETUP.md for field list)
# 3. Paste your project ID below (the subdomain from your MockAPI URL)
# Leave as-is to use the built-in fallback data (app works without this)
EXPO_PUBLIC_MOCKAPI_BASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_ID.mockapi.io/api/v1

# ── n8n AI Webhooks ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paste your active n8n webhook trigger URLs below.
# These are used by the AI Stylist screen (Style Quiz + Image Search).
# Leave as-is to use local rule-based fallback (app works without this)
EXPO_PUBLIC_N8N_QUIZ_WEBHOOK=https://YOUR_N8N_INSTANCE.ngrok-free.app/webhook/style-quiz
EXPO_PUBLIC_N8N_IMAGE_WEBHOOK=https://YOUR_N8N_INSTANCE.ngrok-free.app/webhook/image-style
